rustdesk-server (1.1.28) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Answer UDP NAT requests on the rendezvous port. TestNatRequest was only
    handled on the TCP paths, so a client that asked over UDP never received
    TestNatResponse and could not learn its observed source port. Clients that
    build UDP candidate addresses for hole punching therefore fell back to TCP
    or relay every time. The UDP handler now replies with the observed source
    port, mirroring the TCP semantics; existing clients are unaffected because
    they only ask over TCP.

 -- majorcheng <major@thu.cn>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0800

rustdesk-server (1.1.27) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Forward unreliable QUIC datagrams between paired relay peers. Stream
    forwarding alone forced any datagram-based carrier to fall back to a
    reliable stream, which reintroduced head-of-line blocking and double
    retransmission for KCP sessions. Datagrams are now relayed unchanged when
    both peers are on QUIC and dropped otherwise, so legacy stream sessions and
    bandwidth limits still apply. The edge to master hop keeps its QUIC
    connection as well, so a two-hop relay forwards datagrams end to end.

 -- majorcheng <major@thu.cn>  Mon, 07 Dec 2026 10:00:00 +0800

rustdesk-server (1.1.26) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Deliver pending QUIC stream data before closing a relay connection.
    Closing with CONNECTION_CLOSE right after a relay pair ended discarded
    bytes that had just been written, so short request/response exchanges
    lost their reply; service results and management metadata replies
    reaching a device through an edge relay failed with "relay closed".
    The relay now finishes the send stream and closes the connection after a
    short grace period.

 -- majorcheng <major@thu.cn>  Sat, 05 Dec 2026 22:00:00 +0800

rustdesk-server (1.1.25) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Take over the local registration when only a federated lease exists for a
    peer. A node that accepted a registration while holding a lease kept the
    lease record, so it answered every heartbeat with request_pk and never
    published its own lease; the master and the console stayed on the previous
    site with an offline peer. An accepted registration now always claims the
    local record when the current one is remote-owned or no longer reachable.

 -- majorcheng <major@thu.cn>  Sat, 05 Dec 2026 20:00:00 +0800

rustdesk-server (1.1.24) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Let an edge relay declare local services again: a declared service ID is
    served locally and takes precedence over the upstream, everything else is
    still forwarded. This lets a leaf act as the egress for specific targets it
    can reach, without exposing a general proxy.
  * Document that a `tcp:` service target may be any address the relay can
    reach, so the allowlist is an explicit egress policy.
  * Accept a RustBot peer registration after its local keypair is rebuilt:
    when the registration UUID matches, a rotation statement signed by the
    peer's SOC_UID-derived recovery key replaces the previous public key, so a
    reflashed device can register at any site without manual cleanup.
  * Judge a registration only against the local peer record. A federated lease
    no longer takes part in the source-address and public-key comparison, and
    it no longer overwrites a locally registered peer that is still reachable.
  * Keep the recovery key in a separate peer_recovery table and carry it in
    federation leases, so every site can verify a later rotation locally.
  * Carry the rotation payload in RegisterPk.old_id; hbb_common's protocol and
    the stock RustDesk registration path are unchanged, and agents that do not
    send the payload keep the existing same-address allowance.

 -- majorcheng <major@thu.cn>  Sat, 05 Dec 2026 18:00:00 +0800

rustdesk-server (1.1.23) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add a named service stream alongside peer relay: a dedicated first
    packet carries a version, service ID, request ID and HMAC admission
    proof, and is recognised before RendezvousMessage is parsed.
  * Forward service streams from an edge relay to its configured upstream,
    and let a master relay map a declared service ID to a local Unix socket
    or loopback TCP endpoint, answering with an explicit result code.
  * Derive the service admission proof from RELAY-BOT-TOKEN-SECRET with its
    own domain string; the relay licence key is not used on this path and
    clients cannot supply a target address.
  * Add RELAY-SERVICES and RELAY-SERVICE-TIMEOUT-MS, refusing to start when
    a service map and a relay upstream are configured together.

 -- majorcheng <major@thu.cn>  Sat, 05 Dec 2026 12:00:00 +0800

rustdesk-server (1.1.22) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add a loopback-only read-only federation directory for local management
    APIs, with bearer authentication, paged peer snapshots and single-peer
    identity lookups.
  * Rewrite a federated RequestRelay to the target edge's local relay and
    refuse the request when no local relay is configured.
  * Stop publishing expired local peers across federation links so a
    reconnect cannot briefly mark offline peers online.
  * Record federation link source addresses and last control observation
    times for site health.

 -- majorcheng <major@thu.cn>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800

rustdesk-server (1.1.21) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add an optional QUIC/UDP relay transport for RustBot peers, reusing the
    existing hbbr UUID pairing so the relay stays a transparent byte pump.
  * Authenticate RustBot relay requests with a per-UUID HMAC token carried in
    RequestRelay.token; stock clients keep sending an empty token.
  * Add RELAY-ROLE, RELAY-QUIC-*, RELAY-UPSTREAM-QUIC-* and
    RELAY-BOT-TOKEN-SECRET, failing closed when QUIC is enabled without a
    token secret. Existing deployments keep the standalone TCP behavior.
  * Prefer IPv6 for the edge-to-master QUIC upstream and fall back to TCP only
    on network failures; certificate, pin, ALPN and token failures never fall
    back.
  * Log the loaded QUIC relay certificate pin at startup so pins can be
    distributed to clients.
  * Publish the QUIC relay UDP port in the Docker image and compose file.

 -- majorcheng <major@thu.cn>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 19:55:00 +0800

rustdesk-server (1.1.20) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Require a fresh registration and a routable address before forwarding
    RequestRelay over UDP, so stale peers can no longer poison the socket.
  * Refuse relay requests for unknown or offline peers with an explicit
    RelayResponse instead of leaving the client waiting for a timeout.
  * Rebuild the UDP listener only after a send failure left a frame buffered,
    and report it separately from listener errors.

